    {
      "ordinal": 17,
      "depth": 2,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "2.2.1",
      "title": "International Head and Deputy International Head",
      "body": "●The International Head holds the responsibility of leading its Committee. This includes presenting the committee’s decisions to the Buhurt International Board, the General Assembly, and the community.\n\n●The International Head presides over meetings, coordinates the agenda, facilitates discussions, and ensures the equal participation of all members.\n\n●Collaborating closely with other Committee’s Members, the International Head ensures that committee decisions and actions align with established goals and guidelines.\n\n●The International Head is elected by the General Assembly of Buhurt International and serves three-year terms.\n\n●The International Head and Deputy International Head must have the accreditation of International within their Committee and have the Conference Head title.\n\n●During meetings, the International Head possesses a vote with a weight of two for decision-making.\n\n●In the event that the International Head is unable to fulfill their duties for a period exceeding three months, the Deputy International Head assumes leadership of the Council.\n\n●The Deputy International Head is nominated by the Council and serves a two-year term, similar to other Council members.\n\n●The Deputy International Head shares the same duties with the International Head.",
